        insight: "The director designs against the room, not the textbook: a first-year plan containing zero capital asks - four priorities funded entirely by re-allocation and discipline. Priority one (the quick win): hotel-capture engineering - scripting, pre-arrival offers, concierge familiarisation - targeting 9% to 13%, owner: spa manager, first milestone in 30 days. Priority two: fill the two vacancies at evidenced market rates, framed not as new cost but as the £54,000 agency line converted into £41,000 of permanent payroll - a saving with better service attached. Priority three: rebooking and membership machinery targeting single-visit share from 70% to 58%, built on coached behaviours and a midweek-fenced membership. Priority four (capability): the scorecard, one-to-one and SOP infrastructure, because the diagnosis found decisions being made from memory. The board page states the deferred items explicitly - the thermal-suite renewal and the treatment-room extension - each with the evidence the year's data collection will add to their eventual cases. The year delivers: capture 13.4%, agency line near zero, membership at 60 by month twelve, and revenue up 9% on no new capital. The following January, the director presents the thermal-suite case - now carrying twelve months of capture, contribution and demand data - and it is approved in one meeting. The plan that asked for nothing had been the investment case all along.",
